 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\n# OAuth2 Client prepare_authorization_request returns incorrect headers and body\n\n## Bug report\n\n**Bug summary**\nWhen using the `prepare_authorization_request` method of OAuth2 clients, the method returns incorrect headers and body values. The method should return a tuple with the authorization URL, headers with content type, and an empty body string, but it's returning different values.\n\n**Code for reproduction**\n\n```python\nfrom oauthlib.oauth2 import WebApplicationClient\n\nclient = WebApplicationClient('client_id_here')\nuri = 'https://example.com/authorize'\nredirect_uri = 'https://my-app.com/callback'\nstate = 'random_state_string'\nscope = 'read write'\n\n# This call returns incorrect values\nurl, headers, body = client.prepare_authorization_request(\n    uri, \n    redirect_url=redirect_uri, \n    state=state, \n    scope=scope\n)\n\nprint(\"Headers:\", headers)  # Should be {'Content-Type': 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded'}\nprint(\"Body:\", body)        # Should be ''\n```\n\n**Actual outcome**\nThe method returns:\n- URL: correctly formatted authorization URL\n- Headers: empty dictionary `{}`\n- Body: `None` instead of an empty string\n\n**Expected outcome**\nThe method should return:\n- URL: correctly formatted authorization URL\n- Headers: `{'Content-Type': 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded'}`\n- Body: `''` (empty string)\n\n**Environment information**\n- Operating system: Ubuntu 20.04\n- Python version: 3.8.5\n- oauthlib version: 3.2.0\n\nThis issue affects all OAuth2 client classes that inherit from the base Client class.\n</issue>\n",
